{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because structures in C can’t have methods, property accessors, or custom initializers,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you often need to write such functionality using global functions. Structures in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Swift can declare methods, property accessors, and initializers. You use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macro to group together related global functions into a single structure type that’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"imported into Swift."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Apply CF_SWIFT_NAME to Related Functions","level":3,"anchor":"Apply-CFSWIFTNAME-to-Related-Functions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The example below shows several functions that are all related to a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Color"},{"type":"text","text":" type."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" macro is applied to each function, giving each one a new name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for Swift that’s nested together under the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Color"},{"type":"text","text":" type:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"occ","code":["Color ColorCreateWithCMYK(float c, float m, float y, float k) CF_SWIFT_NAME(Color.init(c:m:y:k:));","","float ColorGetHue(Color color) CF_SWIFT_NAME(getter:Color.hue(self:));","void ColorSetHue(Color color, float hue) CF_SWIFT_NAME(setter:Color.hue(self:newValue:));","","Color ColorDarkenColor(Color color, float amount) CF_SWIFT_NAME(Color.darken(self:amount:));","","extern const Color ColorBondiBlue CF_SWIFT_NAME(Color.bondiBlue);","","Color ColorGetCalibrationColor(void) CF_SWIFT_NAME(getter:Color.calibration());","Color ColorSetCalibrationColor(Color color) CF_SWIFT_NAME(setter:Color.calibration(newValue:));"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The argument you pass to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" macro uses the same syntax as the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#selector"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expression. You use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" argument to refer to the instance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the method belongs to."}]},{"anchor":"Import-Related-Functions-into-Swift","text":"Import Related Functions into Swift","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s how Swift imports the related functions above into a single type:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension Color {","    init(c: Float, m: Float, y: Float, k: Float)","","    var hue: Float { get set }","","    func darken(amount: Float) -> Color","","    static var bondiBlue: Color","","    static var calibration: Color","}"]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can’t reorder or change the number of arguments for type members imported"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" macro."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"title":"Customizing Your C Code for Swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" macro to group functions that have related behavior."}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Language interoperability","anchor":"Language-interoperability","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/c-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/cxx-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"]}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","role":"collection","title":"Standard Library","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Standard Library","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","abstract":[{"text":"Browse the essential types provided by Swift’s standard library.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/cxx-interoperability":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/cxx-interoperability","title":"C++ Interoperability","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/cxx-interoperability","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Work with standard C++ types.","type":"text"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/c-interoperability":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use imported C types or call C variadic functions."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/c-interoperability","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"C Interoperability","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/c-interoperability"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift","title":"Using Imported C Macros in Swift","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Use imported C-defined macros as constants.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","title":"Using Imported C Functions in Swift","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header."}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","title":"Using Imported C Structs and Unions in Swift","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how Swift represents imported C structures and unions, including types with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bitfields and unnamed fields."}],"type":"topic"}}}